{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\nThe {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain` to define its node-identity type. Its\nerror type is introduced in {cite}`requirements.sdk.errors`:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The *identifier* identifies a particular node in the graph.\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types` obligates `Domain` to define a `NodeId` associated type bounded by exactly `Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. An application domain implements it to supply its node identity. The tests cover this as follows.\n\n- **Bounds.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` contains a generic `check_bounds<G: Domain>` function. It calls `identity::<G::NodeId>()`, where `identity` requires `T: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`. If the trait's `NodeId` bound lost `Clone`, `Eq`, `Send` or `Sync`, this would fail to compile.\n- **No extra bounds.** The fixture `Identity` derives only `Clone, PartialEq, Eq`. It has no `Debug` or `Hash`, so the test would also fail to compile if the trait added a bound beyond those four.\n- **Behaviour with the type.** The same test runs `node_path`, `outgoing_edges` and `load_evidence` on that opaque identity. It asserts that `outgoing_edges` returns repeated and distinct identities in order.\n- **A different kind of identity.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[enum_node_ids_distinguish_requirements_and_source_items_in_one_domain]` uses an enum `NodeId` with two variants. It asserts that the variants compare unequal (`assert_ne!`). It also asserts that ids drive `node_path`, the edges, `read`, and the evidence store and load.\n- **Real implementations and further uses.**\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[habeas_paths_preserve_opaque_segments_and_separate_all_node_kinds]` exercises the real `HabeasDomain` node ids.\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` exercises the real `HabeasDomain` node ids.\n  - `src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[review_graph_delegates_unprepared_sources_and_paths_to_the_domain]` exercises the real node ids.\n  - The agent tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs` and the criteria test `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested` use the `NodeId` type in other flows.\n\nThe requirement states a single type-level contract, and the compile-time bound checks assert it directly. The behavioural tests add runtime evidence that equality and cloning of ids work as the graph needs. I found no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "8f371c4ec7f0c0885da5414a2e1353bd9a2d1a595b7e6b3d293f799812f87832",
